# The client test suite. Railway's vyra-production service builds vyralive.app from the repository
# ROOT with Railpack, which decides what kind of project this is by looking at what it finds there.
# A package.json in the root makes it "Detected Node", and it then aborts the build because no start
# command exists — which is exactly what happened to the Live Goals deploy:
#
#   ↳ Found .dockerignore file, applying filters
#   ⚠ No node package manager detected, using npm
#   ↳ Detected Node
#   ✖ No start command detected.
#
# There is nothing to start. The root package.json exists only so `npm test` can run the jsdom suite;
# the browser loads these files directly and none of them are served by Node. Filtering them out
# restores the static-site detection that builds the Caddy image the Caddyfile describes.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. Unanchored, `package.json` would also match server/package.json
# and tiktok-bridge/package.json and break those builds instead.
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/tests
